# NOTE: public/frames and public/images are deliberately COMMITTED.
#
# They are generated (`npm run assets`), so the instinct is to ignore them. But
# their source cannot be reached from CI: the frame masters are 547 MB of PNGs
# that live on the designer's machine and are not in this repo. A deploy host
# therefore has no way to regenerate them, and ignoring them ships a site whose
# hero canvas is permanently blank.
#
# When the source of a generated asset is not available to the build, the
# generated asset is the source. ~17 MB of WebP, which git and Vercel both
# handle without complaint.

# Downloaded placeholder photography — regenerate with npm run assets:images
.cache
